# See https://docs.github.com/en/get-started/getting-started-with-git/ignoring-files for more about ignoring files.

# compiled output
dist
tmp
out-tsc
*.tsbuildinfo
.expo
.expo-shared

# locally-stored chat attachment uploads (see artifacts/api-server/src/routes/attachments.ts) —
# these are user-uploaded files written to local disk, not build output, but must never be committed
artifacts/api-server/uploads/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The ad video work is local-only and must never be committed or pushed.
#
# This is deliberately broader than "don't commit big files": it covers the
# pipeline source as well as the media it produces. Both ad pipelines, every
# input they read and every file they emit stay on this machine.
#
# Consequences, recorded here so nobody has to rediscover them:
#   - scripts/video-ad and scripts/video-ad-remotion exist in no commit and on
#     no remote. A fresh clone cannot build the ads, and if this machine is
#     lost the pipelines are lost with it. Back them up outside git.
#   - assets/screenshots/ is ignored too, which includes regions.json — the
#     file the Remotion composition imports at build time. That is what makes
#     the pipeline unbuildable from a clone, not an oversight.
#
# An earlier version of this block ignored only the generated media and kept
# assets/screenshots/ tracked for exactly that build reason. Superseded.

# Both ad pipelines, in full — source included.
scripts/video-ad/
scripts/video-ad-remotion/

# Everything they read or write: raw clips, style frames, music beds, the
# screenshot corpus and its regions.json manifest.
assets/

# Rendered cuts.
output/

# Finished exports dropped at the repo root ("Advert vid.mp4" etc). Anchored
# to the root so this cannot reach into artifacts/*/public, where opengraph.jpg
# and any future real app media legitimately live and are tracked.
/*.mp4
/*.mov
/*.webm
/*.wav
/*.m4a

# dependencies
node_modules

